 {
  "id": "c05",
  "commit": "ca0b3ebe7",
  "date": "2026-02-13",
  "message": "feat!: Make `openedx_content` and `openedx_tagging` flat, top-level APIs (#478)\n\nThis completes the restructuring of openedx-learning and its APIs which\nwas started by commit a7f45fc . The final form is:\n\n    src/  # All released packages\n      openedx_tagging/        # The Tagging djangoapp\n      openedx_content/        # The Content djangoapp, formerly \"authoring\"\n      openedx_django_lib/     # Generic Django utils, formely \"openedx_learning.lib\"\n      openedx_core/           # Stub package, just to declare __version__\n\nGoing forward, new high-level django apps will be added as peers of these\npackages.  For example, we expect to have `src/openedx_catalog` and\n`src/openedx_learning`.  New capabilities which fit well into the existing\napplication can be added as internal \"applets\", per ADR 20. The goal is to have\nmanageable number of well-separated django apps at the top level, internally\norganized into applets. The top-level apps are hard to refactor (due to\nmigrations) but the internal applets are very easy to refactor. We use\nimportlinter to enforce boundaries between the djangoapps, as well as between\ntheir internal applets--see the `.importliner` config file.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE for operators: install these apps like this--\n    from openedx_content.settings_api import openedx_content_backcompat_apps_to_install\n    ...\n    INSTALLED_APPS = [\n      ...,\n      \"openedx_tagging\",\n      \"openedx_content\",\n      **openedx_content_backcompat_apps_to_install(),\n      ...\n    ]\n\nBR",
